<title>PORTUGAL: Shares widely dispersed in Portugal EDP sale.</title>
<headline>Shares widely dispersed in Portugal EDP sale.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares at the privatisation of state-controlled utility company EDP-Electricidade de Portugal were so widely dispersed that no single investor will have more than one percent, deputy finance minister Fernando Teixeira dos Santos said.</p>
<p>The government sold off 30 percent of EDP to private and institutional investors in an operation that earned the government more than $2 billion.</p>
<p>The company now has 772,584 shareholders of whom 2,205 are foreigners.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
